---
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<Base
  title="Fabric CLI AI Agent Infrastructure | Jeremy Hoover"
  description="I proposed, designed, and wrote the AI skills, prompts, and agent context that shipped with the Microsoft Fabric CLI at general availability."
>
  <article class="section case-study case-study--green">
    <header class="case-hero">
      <div class="container case-hero__grid">
        <div class="case-hero__main">
        <a href={`${base}/#projects`} class="back"><span class="back-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Back to selected projects</span></a>
        <h1>I built the AI skills that shipped with Fabric CLI</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          People were already using AI assistants to run the Fabric CLI, but the assistants didn't understand Fabric, and everyone was writing their own instructions. Before GA, I proposed a shared set of AI assets, shaped it with the PM, and wrote it: agent context, a custom mode, a prompt, skills, references, and scripts. It's all public.
        </p>

        <div class="outcomes-strip" aria-label="Project outcomes">
          <div class="outcome">
            <span class="outcome__num">March 2026</span>
            <span class="outcome__label">Shipped with Fabric CLI at GA</span>
          </div>
          <div class="outcome">
            <span class="outcome__num">36 files</span>
            <span class="outcome__label">In my main AI assets pull request</span>
          </div>
          <div class="outcome">
            <span class="outcome__num">Public</span>
            <span class="outcome__label">PRs, release notes, and a launch article I co-wrote</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        </div>
        <aside class="glance-card" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
          <h2 id="glance-title">At a glance</h2>
          <dl class="glance">
              <div><dt>Role</dt><dd>Senior Content Designer</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Ownership</dt><dd>I proposed it, designed it, and wrote the files in my PRs</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Collaboration</dt><dd>The Fabric CLI PM and engineering team</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Timeframe</dt><dd>December 2025 &ndash; March 2026</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Status</dt><dd>Shipped at GA. The public repo has kept changing since.</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Evidence</dt><dd>Public PRs, commits, release notes, and the GA article</dd></div>
            </dl>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="case-body">
      <div class="container case-shell">
        <nav class="case-toc" aria-label="Fabric CLI case study sections">
          <ul>
            <li><a href="#gap">The problem</a></li>
            <li><a href="#decision">The decision</a></li>
            <li><a href="#implementation">What I built</a></li>
            <li><a href="#validation">Review and release</a></li>
            <li><a href="#response">How people reacted</a></li>
            <li><a href="#reflection">What I learned</a></li>
          </ul>
        </nav>

        <section id="gap" class="reading-column content-section">
          <h2>The problem</h2>
          <p>The Fabric CLI lets developers run Microsoft Fabric from a terminal. More and more people were hooking it up to GitHub Copilot, Claude, Cursor, and other assistants. Each agent needed enough product context to use the CLI correctly, and users kept writing the same instructions over and over.</p>
          <p>There was no single source of truth. Agents needed to know Fabric's hierarchy, command patterns, authentication, safety rules, and how to check their work. They also needed real workflows, not just a long reference doc.</p>
          <p>I thought the CLI needed one structured set of agent assets, not another pile of one-off prompts.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="reading-column content-section" aria-labelledby="role-title">
          <h2 id="role-title">My role</h2>
          <p>I was the Senior Content Designer on the Fabric CLI team. None of this was in the original release plan. I brought it up because agents were becoming real CLI users, and the line between product guidance, design, and code was moving fast.</p>
          <p>The PM and I set the direction based on what others in the industry were doing, our own experience with the CLI, and feedback from community power users. Then I wrote the files, opened the PRs, and revised them through product and engineering review.</p>
          <p>It took my job from improving specific product experiences to designing how agents use the product.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="decision" class="reading-column content-section">
          <h2>One file wasn't going to cut it</h2>
          <p>We looked at a different folder structure, fewer and broader skills, skipping a core skill, one universal context file, and just using <code>AGENTS.md</code>.</p>
          <p>One file looked simpler. But it would have mixed product context, agent behavior, workflows, and task instructions all together. It also wouldn't handle the different file formats, install paths, and loading rules that Copilot, Claude, and Cursor each use.</p>
          <p>So we split it into four layers. A core skill covers the basics once, and the other skills build on it without repeating the same auth, hierarchy, safety, and command guidance.</p>
        </section>

        <figure class="evidence-figure" aria-labelledby="architecture-caption">
          <div class="architecture" role="img" aria-label="Four connected layers of the Fabric CLI AI asset system: context, modes, prompts, and skills">
            <div class="architecture__item"><span class="architecture__number" aria-hidden="true">01</span><h3>Context</h3><p>Teaches each assistant how Fabric and the CLI work.</p></div>
            <div class="architecture__item"><span class="architecture__number" aria-hidden="true">02</span><h3>Modes</h3><p>Set how a specialized agent behaves and what rules it follows.</p></div>
            <div class="architecture__item"><span class="architecture__number" aria-hidden="true">03</span><h3>Prompts</h3><p>Ready-made starting points for common tasks.</p></div>
            <div class="architecture__item"><span class="architecture__number" aria-hidden="true">04</span><h3>Skills</h3><p>Bundle task guidance, references, and scripts.</p></div>
          </div>
          <figcaption id="architecture-caption">
            <strong>Four layers instead of one big file.</strong> Shared context, agent behavior, prompts, and task skills each live in their own place.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <section id="implementation" class="reading-column content-section">
          <h2>What I implemented</h2>
          <p>My main AI assets pull request added or reorganized 36 files. I wrote the files in it, including:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Tool-specific context for GitHub Copilot, Claude, and Cursor</li>
            <li>A custom Fabric CLI agent mode</li>
            <li>A reusable workspace-creation prompt</li>
            <li>Core and Power BI skills</li>
            <li>Detailed command and scenario references</li>
            <li>Automation scripts for health checks, semantic model refresh, refresh history, and report rebinding</li>
            <li>Repo guidance that points contributors and agents to the right source material</li>
          </ul>
          <p>The repo has changed since GA. The pull request shows exactly what I contributed at launch.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="reading-column content-section" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
          <h2 id="workflow-title">Built around how people actually use it</h2>
          <p>We didn't just guess what agents needed. People in the community were already telling us how they used agents with the CLI, what got them better results, and which skills helped.</p>
          <p>That shaped which skills we did first, how people would get to them, and how it would work across assistants. We kept the release to a core skill, Power BI scenarios, and workspace creation instead of trying to cover every Fabric task.</p>
        </section>

        <figure class="evidence-figure" aria-labelledby="flow-caption">
          <ol class="agent-flow">
            <li><span class="agent-flow__step">1</span><strong>User goal</strong><span>Create or manage a Fabric resource</span></li>
            <li><span class="agent-flow__step">2</span><strong>Tool context</strong><span>Load the right product and CLI model</span></li>
            <li><span class="agent-flow__step">3</span><strong>Prompt or skill</strong><span>Apply task-specific guidance</span></li>
            <li><span class="agent-flow__step">4</span><strong>CLI action</strong><span>Run concise Fabric commands</span></li>
            <li><span class="agent-flow__step">5</span><strong>Verification</strong><span>Check authentication, paths, and results</span></li>
          </ol>
          <figcaption id="flow-caption">
            <strong>From goal to checked result.</strong> The agent loads only the guidance it needs for the task, not a generic prompt or the whole API spec.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <section id="validation" class="content-section">
          <div class="reading-column">
            <h2>Review and release</h2>
            <p>The PM reviewed the direction. Engineering reviewed and tested the code. The PR passed the repo's automated checks before it was approved and merged.</p>
            <p>It shipped with the Fabric CLI GA release. The release notes credit the AI assets, and I co-wrote the GA article with the PM about why the CLI was becoming something agents run.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="proof-list" aria-label="Public project evidence">
            <a href="https://github.com/microsoft/fabric-cli/pull/176" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span>Primary contribution</span><strong>Inspect AI assets PR #176</strong><small>36 files, review history, checks, and merged commits ↗</small></a>
            <a href="https://github.com/microsoft/fabric-cli/blob/main/.changes/v1.5.0.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span>Release evidence</span><strong>Read the v1.5 release notes</strong><small>Public contribution credit and release date ↗</small></a>
            <a href="https://community.fabric.microsoft.com/t5/Fabric-Updates-Blog/Fabric-CLI-v1-5-is-here-Generally-Available/ba-p/5172135" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span>Product framing</span><strong>Read the co-authored GA article</strong><small>Agent execution model, scenarios, and contributors ↗</small></a>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section id="response" class="content-section">
          <div class="reading-column">
            <h2>The public response</h2>
            <p>People outside Microsoft didn't talk about it as extra docs. They talked about it as a change in what the CLI could do.</p>
          </div>
          <figure class="response-quote">
            <blockquote>
              “The agent execution layer is the piece I’m most excited about. We’ve been building
              agent-driven Fabric workflows at DataMartIn, and a CLI purpose-built for assistants
              to operate it fluently changes everything.”
            </blockquote>
            <figcaption><strong>Martin Rojze</strong><span>Public response to the Fabric CLI GA announcement</span></figcaption>
          </figure>
          <div class="reading-column">
            <p>Leon Gordon said something similar: that it turned a developer tool into something agents use. That's not an adoption number, but it shows people got it and saw how it fit their work.</p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="reading-column content-section" aria-labelledby="next-title">
          <h2 id="next-title">What happened next</h2>
          <p>After GA, product and engineering started asking a new question: which repeated workflows should become skills next?</p>
          <p>After the release, I also built internal skills for the engineering teams I supported. Same idea, different problems. That's a separate story, so I've kept it out of this one.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="reflection" class="reading-column content-section">
          <h2>What I learned</h2>
          <p>Teaching an agent a list of commands is the easy part. The real work was setting up something we could maintain, that tied together product knowledge, task guidance, per-tool setup, and checking results.</p>
          <p>I think it also shows how design jobs are changing. This took product judgment, information architecture, interaction design, technical writing, writing code in the repo, and working closely with engineering. My title mattered a lot less than seeing what was missing and getting it into the product.</p>
        </section>

        <aside class="inspect-work" aria-labelledby="inspect-title">
          <div>
            <h2 id="inspect-title">Inspect the work</h2>
            <p>The pull request, release notes, and launch article are all public.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="inspect-work__actions">
            <a href="https://github.com/microsoft/fabric-cli/pull/176" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn">View AI assets PR<Icon name="arrow-outward" /></a>
            <a href="https://community.fabric.microsoft.com/t5/Fabric-Updates-Blog/Fabric-CLI-v1-5-is-here-Generally-Available/ba-p/5172135" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn--outline">Read GA article<Icon name="arrow-outward" /></a>
          </div>
        </aside>

        <hr class="divider" />
        <nav class="case-pagination" aria-label="Case study navigation">
          <a href={`${base}/work/org-ai-initiatives`} class="case-pagination__link">
            <span class="case-pagination__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="case-pagination__content"><span class="case-pagination__direction">Previous project</span><span class="case-pagination__title">Org AI initiatives</span></span>
          </a>
          <a href={`${base}/work/statecraft-israel`} class="case-pagination__link case-pagination__link--next">
            <span class="case-pagination__content"><span class="case-pagination__direction">Next project</span><span class="case-pagination__title">Statecraft: Israel</span></span>
            <span class="case-pagination__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .case-study { padding-top: 0; }
  .tag { display: inline-block; margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  h1 { margin-block: var(--space-4) var(--space-6); }
  .lede { max-width: 58ch; margin-bottom: var(--space-12); font-size: var(--size-xl); line-height: 1.6; }
  .outcome { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-1); transition: transform 180ms ease, box-shadow 180ms ease; }
  .outcome__num { font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 13cqw, 2rem); line-height: 1.1; white-space: nowrap; }
  .outcome__label { max-width: 24ch; font-size: var(--size-sm); color: var(--muted); }
  .case-shell { max-width: calc(var(--narrow) + 6rem); }
  .reading-column { width: 100%; max-width: var(--narrow); margin-inline: auto; }
  .content-section { scroll-margin-top: 90px; }
  .content-section h2, .case-summary h2 { margin-bottom: var(--space-6); }
  .content-section:not(:first-child) h2 { margin-top: var(--space-16); }
  .content-section p { margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  .content-section ul { margin: var(--space-4) 0 var(--space-6) var(--space-6); }
  .content-section li { margin-bottom: var(--space-2); }
  code { padding: 0.15em 0.4em; border-radius: 3px; background: var(--portfolio-blue-soft); color: var(--portfolio-ink); font-family: var(--f-mono); font-size: 0.875em; }
  .case-meta { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--space-3); }
  .case-meta div { padding: var(--space-6); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 12px; background: #fff; transition: transform 180ms ease, box-shadow 180ms ease; }
  .case-meta dt { margin-bottom: var(--space-2); color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; text-transform: none; }
  .case-meta dd { color: var(--portfolio-ink); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  .case-toc { max-width: var(--narrow); margin: var(--space-8) auto var(--space-16); padding-block: var(--space-6); border-block: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .case-toc__label { display: block; margin-bottom: var(--space-3); color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.6875rem; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.2; text-transform: none; }
  .case-toc ul { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem 0; margin: 0; list-style: none; }
  .case-toc li { --toc-divider: var(--border); display: flex; align-items: center; }
  .case-toc li + li { margin-left: var(--space-4); }
  .case-toc li + li::before { content: ''; width: 2px; height: 16px; margin-right: var(--space-4); border-radius: 999px; background: var(--toc-divider); }
  .case-toc li:nth-child(3n) { --toc-divider: var(--border); }
  .case-toc li:nth-child(3n + 1) { --toc-divider: var(--border); }
  .case-toc a { display: inline-flex; min-height: 32px; align-items: center; color: var(--portfolio-ink); font-size: 0.875rem; font-weight: 650; line-height: 1.3; text-decoration: none; }
  .case-toc a:hover { color: var(--portfolio-blue); text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-color: var(--portfolio-blue); text-decoration-thickness: 2px; text-underline-offset: 5px; }
  .evidence-figure { width: 100%; max-width: var(--narrow); margin: var(--space-12) auto var(--space-16); }
  .evidence-figure figcaption { width: 100%; max-width: none; margin-top: var(--space-4); color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--size-sm); }
  .evidence-figure figcaption strong { color: var(--portfolio-ink); }
  .architecture { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--space-3); padding: var(--space-4); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; background: var(--portfolio-blue-soft); }
  .architecture__item { position: relative; min-height: 210px; padding: var(--space-6); border: 1px solid rgba(16,26,45,0.1); border-radius: 14px; background: #fff; transition: transform 180ms ease, box-shadow 180ms ease; }
  .architecture__item::after { content: '→'; position: absolute; top: 50%; right: -1.05rem; z-index: 1; display: grid; width: 1.55rem; height: 1.55rem; place-items: center; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--portfolio-blue); color: #fff; font-weight: 800; transform: translateY(-50%); }
  .architecture__item:last-child::after { content: none; }
  .architecture__number { display: block; margin-bottom: var(--space-8); color: var(--portfolio-coral); font-family: var(--f-heading); font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: 0.08em; }
  .architecture h3 { margin-bottom: var(--space-2); color: var(--portfolio-blue); }
  .architecture p { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  .agent-flow { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--space-2); margin: 0; padding: var(--space-4); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; background: var(--surface-tint); list-style: none; }
  .agent-flow li { position: relative; display: flex; min-height: 170px; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-2); padding: var(--space-4); border-radius: 12px; background: #fff; color: var(--muted); transition: transform 180ms ease, box-shadow 180ms ease; }
  .agent-flow li::after { content: '→'; position: absolute; top: 50%; right: -0.75rem; z-index: 1; color: var(--portfolio-blue); font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 800; transform: translateY(-50%); }
  .agent-flow li:last-child::after { content: none; }
  .agent-flow__step { display: grid; width: 1.75rem; height: 1.75rem; place-items: center; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--portfolio-blue); color: #fff; font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 800; }
  .agent-flow strong { color: var(--portfolio-ink); font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .agent-flow li > span:last-child { font-size: 0.8rem; line-height: 1.45; }
  .proof-list { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); width: 100%; max-width: var(--narrow); gap: var(--space-3); margin: var(--space-8) auto 0; }
  .proof-list a { display: flex; min-height: 176px; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; gap: var(--space-3); padding: var(--space-6); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 14px; background: #fff; transition: transform 180ms ease, box-shadow 180ms ease; }
  .proof-list a:hover { text-decoration: none; box-shadow: 0 8px 20px rgba(16,26,45,0.08); border-color: rgba(17,85,204,0.35); }
  .proof-list span { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 600; text-transform: none; }
  .proof-list strong { color: var(--portfolio-ink); font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.35; }
  .proof-list small { margin-top: auto; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.8rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  .response-quote { width: 100%; max-width: var(--narrow); margin: var(--space-8) auto; }
  .response-quote blockquote { margin: 0; padding: var(--space-8); border-radius: 0 16px 16px 0; background: #fff; color: var(--portfolio-ink); font-family: var(--f-heading); font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 2.5vw, 1.5rem); font-style: normal; line-height: 1.5; transition: transform 180ms ease, box-shadow 180ms ease; }
  .response-quote figcaption { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.1rem; padding: var(--space-3) 0 0 var(--space-8); color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--size-sm); }
  .response-quote figcaption strong { color: var(--portfolio-ink); }
  .inspect-work { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.4fr) minmax(220px, 0.6fr); width: 100%; max-width: var(--narrow); gap: var(--space-8); align-items: center; margin: var(--space-16) auto 0; padding: clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 3rem); border-radius: 20px; background: var(--portfolio-blue); }
  .inspect-work .tag { color: var(--portfolio-yellow); }
  .inspect-work h2 { margin-bottom: var(--space-3); color: #fff; }
  .inspect-work p { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.82); }
  .inspect-work__actions { display: grid; gap: var(--space-3); }
  .inspect-work .btn { display: flex; min-height: 48px; align-items: center; justify-content: center; background: var(--portfolio-coral); color: #fff; text-align: center; }
  .inspect-work .btn:hover { background: #e85f43; }
  .inspect-work .btn--outline { border-color: rgba(255,255,255,0.7); background: transparent; color: #fff; }
  .inspect-work .btn--outline:hover { border-color: #fff; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.1); }
  .divider { margin-block: var(--space-16) var(--space-8); }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .case-toc ul { gap: 0.5rem 1.5rem; }
    .case-toc li + li { margin-left: 0; }
    .case-toc li + li::before { content: none; }
    .architecture { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
    .architecture__item { min-height: 180px; }
    .architecture__item::after { content: none; }
    .agent-flow { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
    .agent-flow li { min-height: 145px; }
    .agent-flow li::after { content: none; }
    .proof-list { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .proof-list a { min-height: 0; }
    .proof-list small { margin-top: 0; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .content-section { scroll-margin-top: 130px; }
    .case-meta { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .case-meta div { padding: var(--space-4); }
    .case-toc { margin-top: var(--space-6); margin-bottom: var(--space-12); padding-block: var(--space-4); }
    .case-toc ul { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); width: 100%; gap: var(--space-1) var(--space-6); }
    .case-toc a { min-height: 44px; }
    .architecture { grid-template-columns: 1fr; padding: var(--space-3); }
    .architecture__item { min-height: auto; }
    .architecture__number { margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
    .agent-flow { grid-template-columns: 1fr; padding: var(--space-3); }
    .agent-flow li { min-height: auto; }
    .response-quote blockquote { padding: var(--space-6); }
    .response-quote figcaption { padding-left: var(--space-6); }
    .inspect-work { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .outcome:hover,
    .case-meta div:hover,
    .architecture__item:hover,
    .agent-flow li:hover,
    .proof-list a:hover,
    .response-quote blockquote:hover { transform: none; }
  }

  /* ---- Visual refresh ---- */
  /* stepper: numbered nodes on one line */
  .agent-flow { --node: 36px; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 0.75rem; padding: 0; border: 0; background: transparent; list-style: none; }
  .agent-flow li { position: relative; display: flex; min-height: 0; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: 0.35rem; padding: 0; border: 0; border-radius: 0; background: transparent; box-shadow: none; text-align: center; }
  .agent-flow li > span:first-child { position: relative; z-index: 1; display: grid; width: var(--node); height: var(--node); margin-bottom: 0.6rem; place-items: center; border: 3px solid #fff; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--portfolio-blue); box-shadow: var(--elev-1); color: #fff; font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 800; }
  .agent-flow li::after { content: ''; position: absolute; top: calc(var(--node) / 2); left: 50%; z-index: 0; width: calc(100% + 0.75rem); height: 2px; background: var(--portfolio-blue-soft); transform: translateY(-50%); }
  .agent-flow li:last-child::after { content: none; }
  .agent-flow li::before { content: none; }
